  "sourceNotes": "Jalfrezi (sometimes jhal frezi) is a Bengali dry-fry curry technique adapted in British curry houses to include pepper and tomato. The word comes from Bengali and means hot fry. It became one of the most popular curries in British restaurants in the 1990s and 2000s, often ranked alongside tikka masala in surveys of British curry preferences. Pat Chapman, The Curry Club Indian Restaurant Cookbook (Piatkus Books, 1984): first widely available British reference for the restaurant version.",
